{title: Amazing Grace}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: G}
{tempo: 90}
{time: 3/4}

# Public domain: lyrics John Newton (1779), melody "New Britain" (traditional)
# Simple beginner arrangement in G using G, G7, C, D

{start_of_verse}
A[G]mazing grace, how [G7]sweet the [C]sound
That [G]saved a wretch like [D]me
I [G]once was [G7]lost, but [C]now am [G]found
Was [D]blind, but [G]now I see
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
'Twas [G]grace that [G7]taught my [C]heart to [G]fear
And [G]grace my fears re[D]lieved
How [G]precious [G7]did that [C]grace ap[G]pear
The [D]hour I [G]first believed
{end_of_verse}
